I realized that most of the arguments I use when talking about
contextuality in Lojban come from "Formality of Language: definition,
measurement and behavioral determinants" by F. Heylighen
(http://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/download?doi=10.1.1.30.6280&rep=rep1&type=pdf)
which I read many years ago. Section 2 seems most relevant to me.

Just in case anyone could find it interesting too.

